current visual review, governance audit, and closure remained open\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-09T08-58-28-UfXz-competitive_intelligence_workflow_phase10_r13k_f07_pause.md (cwd=/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow, rollout_path=/Users/smkzw/.codex/sessions/2026/08/09/rollout-2026-08-09T16-58-28-019fe5be-b687-7e11-8c76-2b2c0d2126c9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T03:49:29+00:00, thread_id=019fe5be-b687-7e11-8c76-2b2c0d2126c9, R13k candidate and no-loss F07 pause)\n\n### keywords\n\n- R13k, Task 10.3, F07, `task-10.3-20260902-r13k`, `run_a90a2500314fafd8ec4885fd`, `pre-rc-run_557186bed2e4368b296bda17`, ego-lite, `baseline-disease-context`, `subgroups-supporting-evidence`, `暂无公开记录（基线）`, MiniMax, `checkpoint_20260902_full_matrix_pass_visual_review_paused.md`, `PAUSE_HANDOFF_20260902_114643.md`\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when reviewing the reports, the user asked for richer click-through: bubble charts should open detailed efficacy/safety cards or full drug profiles; “absent AESI content should not be forced into display” -> prioritize meaningful drill-down and keep genuinely absent evidence out of the visible report. [Task 1] [skysight memory]\n- Symptom: a long-running Cursor self-test or Qoder loop vanishes after a wait, while reports appear stuck. Cause: the process may have been lost through shell/sandbox/background handling rather than reaching a product conclusion. Fix: inspect PID/process state and persisted logs, relaunch as a tracked background job where needed, and record which Wave checks remain before resuming. [Task 19] [chronicle memory]\n- Symptom: a provider/model looks configured in Hermes or OMP but a route/session still fails. Cause: provider registration, UI catalog, active-session routing, and bridge/session discovery are separate layers. Fix: inspect the selected session/base route and use a real generation or route smoke check; never expose copied credentials in records. [Task 20] [chronicle memory]\n- Symptom: the parent pipeline times out and leaves a diagnosis with no useful UI recovery. Cause: partial/failed child states were conflated with completion or retried without idempotency. Fix: restore state deterministically, distinguish `queued/partial_failed` and `pending/failed` from locked success, prevent duplicate work, and verify the real retry affordance in the browser. [Task 22] [chronicle memory]\n- Symptom: a 5x3 retest is called complete because handoff/ledger files exist or a progress value updates. Cause: monitoring and test-matrix evidence were mistaken for E2E acceptance. Fix: run the runtime entry point, inspect fail-close/retry behavior and actual browser layout, then record any remaining blocked/partial state in the ledger. [Task 23] [chronicle memory]\n\n# Task Group: August 9 competitive-research multi-Skill workflow and Windows Hermes/OMP continuity\n\nscope: Chronicle-observed design decisions for the local competitive-intelligence workflow and a parallel Windows Hermes/OMP remote-deployment recovery path; preserve current scope and do not treat screen observation as release acceptance.\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/竞品调研工作流 and Codex task `规划Windows远程部署Hermes和OMP`; reuse_rule=reopen the current context file, evidence workspace, and live Windows SSH state before continuing.\n\n## Task 1: Refine competitive-research evidence, output, and correction contracts, outcome: design context actively edited; no final workflow release observed [chronicle memory]\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- extensions/chronicle/resources/2026-08-09T15-26-00-gsis-10min-memory-summary.md (cwd=/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/竞品调研工作流, rollout_path=/Users/smkzw/.codex/memories/extensions/chronicle/resources/2026-08-09T15-26-00-gsis-10min-memory-summary.md, updated_at=2026-08-09T15:26:00+00:00, thread_id=None, evidence workspace and output-state observations) [chronicle memory]\n- extensions/chronicle/resources/2026-08-09T15-06-00-